{"type":"message","id":"d2fdb30e","parentId":"9029fdbf","timestamp":"2026-05-19T02:03:24.766Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The root requires auth too. GET /send doesn't make sense so that's expected. The issue is that POST /send with X-API-Key returns 1101 (Worker exception). This means the Cloudflare Worker itself is crashing when trying to process the send request.\n\nLet me try a few more variations to see if I can get the send to work - maybe the body needs a different structure.\n\nActually, wait - looking at the history response structure, I see there's `type: \"message\"` and `replyTo: null` and `echoAsset`. Maybe the send endpoint needs a specific structure. Let me look at what's returned in the history to understand the expected format.\n\nActually, I notice the GET returns messages with fields like `id`, `content`, `threadId`, `type`, `timestamp`, `echoAsset`, `replyTo`. \n\nThe POST body probably just needs `threadId` and `content`, so the 1101 error is likely a server-side bug I can't fix from here. Let me test the send endpoint with minimal parameters to see if it's actually accessible.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7ed402c0-b6d2-4b28-9081-1ed6ba777a2e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":798,"output":311,"cacheRead":19232,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20341,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779156194127,"responseId":"chatcmpl-91d6b8de-38a3-407d-a644-293538d10838"}}
