{"type":"message","id":"faee6564","parentId":"167b7bdc","timestamp":"2026-05-19T02:03:40.978Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even with minimal body it's 1101. The send endpoint itself is broken at the worker level. Let me check if maybe there's a different path like /message or /post. But first, let me try a simple test to see if I get something different.\n\nActually, wait - maybe the issue is that the `X-API-Key` header passes auth but the send route requires different auth. But then I got 401 with Bearer auth for GET endpoints. The fact that X-API-Key passes auth on GET but the POST still 500s suggests auth is fine but the handler itself is crashing.\n\nLet me try another path or method.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-74bf29bb-46f6-4d7c-965e-0cc8b5cb24b0","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different variations\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/message\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1\n\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/post\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":876,"output":302,"cacheRead":19488,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20666,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779156204928,"responseId":"chatcmpl-056fbf25-d014-42f7-bdf4-87028afa9d65"}}
