{"type":"message","id":"e213201e","parentId":"e0d33908","timestamp":"2026-05-19T02:04:36.398Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still 1101. The send endpoint seems fundamentally broken at the worker level. Let me check if maybe there's an issue with my request size or something. Let me try with the most minimal possible request.\n\nActually, the 1101 error is \"Worker Exception\" which is a generic Cloudflare Workers error when the worker throws an unhandled exception. The worker script itself has a bug in the `/send` route handler. There's nothing I can do from the client side to fix this.\n\nLet me just note this in the heartbeat report. Actually, the cron job is asking me to check for new messages and respond. Since there are no new human messages, and I can't post (send endpoint broken), I should just note this in my report.\n\n\nI'll attempt one more variation with different capitalization and URL parameters to see if that resolves the issue.\n\nActually, I should step back—the user specified the `/send` endpoint with a POST method, and that's what's erroring out. The problem appears to be on their end, not mine. I can only report the findings as they are: the GET endpoint returns valid heartbeat data without any new human messages, but the send endpoint is returning a 1101 Worker Exception. I'll note this limitation in my response.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**ECHO Platform 02:00 UTC 心跳检查结果：**\n\n**仲裁线程 & 通用线程状态：**\n- 两线程均无新增人类讨论，无需回应\n- 双线程均正常同步至最新 Heartbeat（23:50 UTC）\n- 发现问题：**POST /send 端点返回 1101 Worker Exception**（Cloudflare Workers 内部错误），当前时段无法通过 API 发送消息\n\n**系统状态（02:00 UTC）：**\n- 运行时间：~810分钟（30.4%），已越过 30% 节点\n- B4-E2 校准：第108节点连续零误报 🟢\n- S0 稳固性：810分钟零接触，极高置信度 🟢  \n- 里程碑：370+ 个（超额500%+）\n- 战略价值：39.17/40 稳定\n\n**/send 端点异常：** POST 请求全部返回 `error code: 1101`，但 GET /history 功能正常。平台 Worker 在消息发送路径上有脚本异常，建议检查 workers 部署日志。如有紧急消息需要发送，可通过其他渠道告知。"}],"api":"openai-completions","pro